// TEAR SEED -- an author-owned INITIAL GUESS for this recycle stream.  A recycle
// loop has no upstream to propagate from, so the student seeds the tear; the
// solver (Wegstein/Newton on the tear) CONVERGES it -- the values below are a
// starting estimate, NOT a specification.  The no-silent-crutch credo: the seed
// is visible and yours to own.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*--- Choupo stream state.  Every DIMENSIONAL value carries its unit; the parser converts to SI.
     componentMolarFlows is the OVERALL material (all phases); a phases{} block, when present,
     is a decomposition that sums back to it exactly. ---*/

componentMolarFlows
{
    N2    7959.133697 kmol/h;
    H2    24084.79879 kmol/h;
    NH3    540.3069209 kmol/h;
    Ar    1115.528171 kmol/h;
}

T               250 K;
P               20000000 Pa;
phase           gas;
// The seed is the separator's VAPOUR and it feeds recycleComp, which refuses
// liquid in its suction (2026-10-21, DEV.md 4c).  A tear seed is the
// compressor's inlet on the FIRST pass and is read as it carries (a produced
// stream keeps its producer's answer), so its phase is DECLARED here, as
// greenAmmoniaPEQ_baseCase's and evaporator05's seeds declare theirs; without
// it the seed carries the struct default, vf = 0, and the first pass reads
// 33 700 kmol/h of liquid.  The solver overwrites it from the second pass on.
